# The version decides across Batches; the timestamp orders events within one Batch.
@run = 1
@id = order-{{run}}

### One Batch, events listed out of timestamp order: sorted, so v1 then v2 both apply
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 2, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:05:00Z", "payload": { "title": "v2" } },
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "v1" } }
]

### Read it: version 2
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}

### Jump ahead to v5
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 5, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:10:00Z", "payload": { "title": "v5" } }
]

### Late v3 with a newer timestamp: SkippedStale, the version wins over the clock
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 3, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T12:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "v3 arrived late" } }
]

### Read it: still version 5
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}
